Description: Fix crash when popup window has null transientParent
 The patch fix-set-lastInputDevice-on-pointer-and-keyboard-enter.patch
 accidentally removed the transientParent guard along with the
 lastInputDevice() guard from the Qt::Popup branch in
 QWaylandXdgSurface constructor. This causes a null pointer
 dereference in QWaylandXdgSurface::createPositioner() when a
 Qt::Popup window has no transientParent (e.g. QCompleter popup,
 QTBUG-130474).
 .
 This patch restores the transientParent guard while keeping the
 lastInputDevice() guard removed as intended by the original patch.
Origin: vendor
Bug: https://pms.uniontech.com/bug-view-380865.html
Forwarded: not-needed

Index: qt6-wayland/src/plugins/shellintegration/xdg-shell/qwaylandxdgshell.cpp
===================================================================
--- qt6-wayland.orig/src/plugins/shellintegration/xdg-shell/qwaylandxdgshell.cpp
+++ qt6-wayland/src/plugins/shellintegration/xdg-shell/qwaylandxdgshell.cpp
@@ -314,7 +314,7 @@ QWaylandXdgSurface::QWaylandXdgSurface(Q
 
     if (type == Qt::ToolTip && transientParent) {
         setPopup(transientParent);
-    } else if (type == Qt::Popup) {
+    } else if (type == Qt::Popup && transientParent) {
         setGrabPopup(transientParent, display->lastInputDevice(), display->lastInputSerial());
     } else {
         setToplevel();
